  "ingredients": [
    "14 egg yolks",
    "1 pint sour cream",
    "2 teaspoons vanilla extract",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "0.5 cup butter",
    "8 cups all-purpose flour",
    "1.5 cups shortening",
    "0.33333298563957 cup confectioners' sugar for decoration"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "In a large bowl mix together all ingredients. Stir into a ball, then turn dough out onto a floured surface . Knead dough for 1/2 hour. If you have a mixer with a dough hook attachment, mix for about 15 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Let dough rest for 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "On a floured surface, roll out dough to 1/4 to 1/8 inch thickness. Cut into strips that are 3 inches long and 1 inch wide. In the center of each strip, cut a 1 inch slit, lengthwise. Pull one end of the strip through the slit to form a bow.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "In a frying pan or an electric skillet, melt shortening and heat to about 350 degrees F (175 degrees C). in a frying pan this would be on medium high heat.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Place cookies in hot oil. Cook on both sides until lightly browned then remove to a paper towel.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Dust finished cookies with confectioners sugar.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    }
  ],
